(113891, 5039, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background4,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,<br/>Challenge: Does your entry meet it?4,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 3,<br/>Total Averaged Rating4.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background4,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,Challenge: Does your entry meet it?4,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 3,Total Averaged Rating4.   Autool', '2002-09-01 10:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(113892, 5039, 3080, '<td valign="top">This is some interesting effects you tried here, but I don''t know as if it apeals to me.  the lighting is good for the effect used.  The angle is ok, might have a more visual impact if the middle of the ball were centered in the photo.  Colors are very nice, and reference to childhood is very strong.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is some interesting effects you tried here, but I don''t know as if it apeals to me.  the lighting is good for the effect used.  The angle is ok, might have a more visual impact if the middle of the ball were centered in the photo.  Colors are very nice, and reference to childhood is very strong.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-09-01 14:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(113893, 5039, 2932, '<td valign="top">For the few of you that were curious, the effect here was to rotate the beachball a 1/2 turn during the exposure, using a strobe light to produce discrete wedges of color rather than a blur.  The beachball had 6 sections: red, white, blue, while, yellow, white.  Since those are primary colors, I got quite a colorful shot.  <br/><br/>In fact, beachballs as I remember them from my childhood were very colorful.<br/><br/>Some outtakes are available at //www.geocities.com/owennnnn/makingof/beachball/</td>', 'For the few of you that were curious, the effect here was to rotate the beachball a 1/2 turn during the exposure, using a strobe light to produce discrete wedges of color rather than a blur.  The beachball had 6 sections: red, white, blue, while, yellow, white.  Since those are primary colors, I got quite a colorful shot.  In fact, beachballs as I remember them from my childhood were very colorful.Some outtakes are available at //www.geocities.com/owennnnn/makingof/beachball/', '2002-09-02 02:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(113894, 5039, 2217, '<td valign="top">I gave yours my highest vote. I simply loved your picture, I am rather sad that your picture rated so low, it such wonderful picture which I think should have rated much higher.</td>', 'I gave yours my highest vote. I simply loved your picture, I am rather sad that your picture rated so low, it such wonderful picture which I think should have rated much higher.', '2002-09-03 09:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
